# aml_autoscript.src — source for the USB stick's aml_autoscript uImage.
#
# Built with:
#   mkimage -A arm64 -O linux -T script -C none -d aml_autoscript.txt aml_autoscript
#
# The payload is aml_autoscript.txt: this file's commands with the comments
# stripped, because the payload is run by U-Boot's hush parser and a comment
# with an unbalanced quote in it hangs the parser. Keep the two in step -
# change a command here, change it there, and rebuild.
#
# Note the header's timestamp is the build time, so rebuilding produces a
# different 64-byte header even when the payload is identical. Compare
# payloads, not files, when checking a rebuild.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# The vendor's own aml_autoscript (from the factory image) sets a multi-boot
# order — sd, usb, emmc, org — and then runs bootscript/cfgload/s905_autoscript/
# boot.scr. Those scripts are written for a DIFFERENT kernel (the 6.18.55
# mainline one) and a different device tree. On this box they select a mainline
# DTB that describes 4 GB of RAM, which the 2 GB board does not have, and the
# kernel dies before any console output at all.
#
# This script does the minimum that works: load OUR kernel and OUR device tree
# from the stick and boot them, with root on the stick's own second partition.
# It is self-contained — no box-config dependency, no boot order, no fallback
# to a broken kernel.
#
# The boot artefacts live at the ROOT of the FAT boot partition (not in d/),
# so the paths here are flat: "Image" and "sc2_s905x4_ah212_linux.dtb".
#
# init= selects the init system. systemd gives a real multi-user system.
# /root/rescue-init.sh is ALSO installed on the stick and is a working
# fallback: if systemd ever fails, interrupt the boot at the U-Boot prompt
# (bootdelay=3 gives you a window) and change init= to /root/rescue-init.sh.
#
# NOTE the single quotes around bootargs. Escaped double quotes store literal
# backslashes, which corrupts the kernel command line and resets the CPU.
#
# The payload is executed by U-Boot's hush parser, so it must not contain
# quotes in comments: an unbalanced quote puts the parser into its ">"
# continuation prompt and the script never runs. The commented version of
# this file is kept as documentation; the uImage is built from a
# comment-stripped copy.
#
# This file is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE in the repository root). The kernel
# and DTB it loads are GPL-2.0 — see kernel/GPL-2.0-NOTICE.md.

usb start 0
fatload usb 0:1 0x2000000 Image
fatload usb 0:1 0x5000000 sc2_s905x4_ah212_linux.dtb
setenv bootargs 'root=/dev/sda2 rootfstype=ext4 rootwait rw console=ttyS0,921600 earlycon=amlogic,meson-uart,0xfe07a000 no_console_suspend nowatchdog pd_ignore_unused clk_ignore_unused TERM=vt220 maxcpus=4 init=/lib/systemd/systemd'
booti 0x2000000 - 0x5000000
